course: dictionary
lesson: 10004
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word teller can mean a person who works at a bank, a person who tells stories, or a person who counts votes. The clues around the word show you which meaning is meant.
explain: «She works as a bank teller and takes in the money all morning.» The words bank and money tell you the teller works at a counter. «The storyteller sat by the fire and told tales of brave knights.» The word before -teller is the clue: a storyteller tells stories.
explain: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right. Always read the whole sentence first, because the same word can mean different things in different places.
fact: A teller is a person who tells something, such as a storyteller or a fortune-teller.
fact: A bank teller works at a bank counter, taking in money and paying it out.
fact: ATM stands for automated teller machine; in the UK it is often called a cash machine.
fact: A teller can also be a person who counts the votes in an election or meeting.
fact: The word teller often appears in compound words, like storyteller and fortune-teller, so look at the other half of the word for a clue.
exercise: «She works as a bank teller, counting money all day at the counter.» What is a teller in this sentence? | A person who counts votes in an election | A machine that prints tickets | A person who tells stories to children | *A person who works at a bank counter
exercise: «The storyteller sat by the fire and told tales of brave knights.» What is a storyteller? | A person who sells books | *A person who tells stories out loud | A person who works in a bank | A person who counts votes
exercise: «The votes were counted by the teller at the meeting.» Who is the teller here? | A bank worker | A fortune-teller | A storyteller | *A person who counts the votes
test: «The fortune teller said bad luck was coming, and the man paid her every week.» What does fortune teller mean? | *A person who claims to tell what will happen in the future | A person who works at a bank counter | A person who counts votes at a meeting | A person who tells bedtime stories to children
test: In ATM, what does the T stand for? | *Teller | Tall | Ticket | Trust
exam: «Aesop was an ancient Greek teller of animal stories.» What does teller mean here? | A bank worker | A person who counts votes | A person who predicts the future | *A person who tells stories
